---
title: "Brian's Empanadas"
description: "Authentic Argentine beef empanadas, a traditional recipe from a true Argentinian."
category: 'Main Dish'
makes: 'About 20 empanadas'
author: ["Brian"]
tags: ['argentine', 'beef', 'meat', 'savory pastry','street food']

portions: 5
---

## Shortcrust Pastry ->&dough

[Heat] In a #saucepan, the @water{150 ml}, @salt{1/2 tsp}, and @butter{100 g}. ->&butter mixture{} // Remove from heat as soon as the butter melts and let cool.

[Knead] Incorporate this &butter mixture{} into the @flour{500 g}. Work it to form a ball. // Moisten with an extra splash of water if the dough does not bind well

[Rest] Cover with #plastic wrap{} touching the surface. Chill in the refrigerator for at least ~_{30 min}.

## Filling ->&filling

[Sweat] The @onions{200 g}(finely diced) with a drizzle of @oil until translucent.

[Incorporate] The @red bell pepper{1/2}(finely diced).

[Sear] Add the @ground beef{200 g} over ^{high heat}.

[Season] With @salt{1/2 tsp}, @garlic{2 cloves}(pressed), @fresh oregano{1 tsp}, @sweet paprika{1 tsp}, and @fresh parsley{1 tbsp}. // Argentine grandmother's rule: 1 clove of garlic per 100g of meat

[Mix] Remove from heat, stir in the @eggs{2}(hard-boiled, finely diced) and some @green olives{}.

## Baking

[Roll out] The &dough with a #rolling pin{}.

[Cut out] Dough circles using a #pastry cutter{}.

[Shape] Place the &filling on half of each circle. Fold into a half-moon shape and pinch the edges firmly to seal the dough. // Prick the top with a toothpick to create a small steam vent

[Bake] At ^{200C} for about ~baking{15 min}. // Stop baking as soon as they are nicely golden brown
